{
  "format": "autoyou.peer-verification/1",
  "purpose": "Cross-implementation conformance vectors for the Nearby verification code. shared/peer_verification.py is the reference; PeerVerificationCode.swift must produce identical rows. Generated from the reference, so a vector cannot bless a bug.",
  "notes": [
    "Codes are order-independent: swapping local and remote must not change the row.",
    "The alphabet is a security parameter. It must be exactly 64 unique symbols so each contributes exactly six bits.",
    "Six symbols, not four: four is 24 bits, which an attacker in the middle can grind offline inside a ten-minute invitation."
  ],
